# Core source findings and deferred handoff — draft

**Draft: source reconciliation is complete; editing, independent review and Pass‑1 closeout remain
pending.** This handoff accounts for **185 original candidates: 103 Core-family and 82 boundary
candidates**, with every original ID and exact-scope inherited outcome preserved. These are source
concerns and traceability records, rather than accepted bug counts. No new `CORE-DOC-*`/`CORE-IMP-*`
layer was needed: references use `core-001:<original-ID>#documentation`, `#engineering`, `#decision`
or `#qualification`. A reference labels evidence and responsibility; it accepts no unrun claim.

The original source pin remains **`fe342fb0b6fdc4087ed4cbe4ee292e5039f5a7ef`**. Current primary comments
legitimately include the accepted discovery/crypto edits. Original source/range checks therefore use
pinned Git blobs and recorded BOM/newline representations, independently of current documentation hashes.
The earlier preliminary/full-family maps, reports, helpers and results remain byte-identical.

**Stopping point:** finish and publish Core Pass 1 with this deferred-finding handoff, then stop.
This document is findings/status/evidence, not a Pass‑2 plan, implementation assignment, experiment
plan, new tooling project or permission for physical work.

