## Latest qualified review authority

The full source definitions stay historical. Fresh editors and the final verifier should use the
qualified successors, rather than repeating an initial report's inaccurate locator or assurance.

- **A:** accepted revision-2 review permits stale groups to persist; no one-scan/age-based convergence
  is promised. Null-resolver assertions establish this SDK's current choice, rather than OS impossibility.
- **C:** accepted revision-2 review scopes local AES key/IV clearing to entry into the protected scope.
  CBC's second pre-try allocation can fail after the key copy exists. The latest accepted BER,
  supplied-Q and AsnWriter qualifications remain: inspected X.690 reading is complete; supplying Q skips
  the checked .NET v10.0.0 absent-Q extraction; Encode retains writer storage and Reset clears its written
  prefix. Actual installed runtime/native cleanup remains separately qualified.
- **Protocol R1:** in retained SCP11 **1.3.0.13 Public Review**, a/c request is **§7.6.2.3** and response
  **§7.6.3.1/Table 7-18**; b request is **§7.7.2.3** and response **§7.7.3.1/Table 7-22**. INTERNAL
  AUTHENTICATE is **§7.7**; **§7.1.1** describes parameter coding. SCP03 **1.1.2 Public Release** response
  is **§7.1.1.6/Table 7-3**, with 29 mandatory bytes plus its conditional three-byte counter; the explicit
  initial EXTERNAL AUTHENTICATE zero-chain rule is **§6.2.3**. Initial combined request/response locators
  remain preserved input limitations, not the authority for new wording.
- **Protocol R2:** null firmware fails configured-processor admission before the support branch.
  Broad exception tests establish neither that support branching nor a handshake was reached.
- **Protocol R3:** protected 9000/62xx/63xx claims retain **R-MAC selected** applicability; Core SCP03
  selects `0x33`. The inspected **§6.2.6** empty-command/counter rule applies when **C-DECRYPTION and
  C-MAC are both required**. The error-status-only rule, genuine EXTERNAL AUTHENTICATE exception and
  current instruction-only later-INS82 concern remain separate. Current fake/Python padding agreement
  supplies no independent resolution of the selected encryption-path discrepancy.
- **Protocol R4:** two 32-byte P-256 agreements concatenate to **64 bytes**; X9.63 then derives
  **80 bytes**, split into five 16-byte values. This is a qualified source width correction, not a
  recomputed crypto result.
- **FIDO review:** current CTAP peer helper checks coordinates/P-256 provider import, without all
  required peer COSE labels. A prescriptive strict-profile target is different from implemented checks.
  Scripted token acquisition/reuse tests establish the SDK choice, not authenticator acceptance.

Protocol correction/qualification authority is the completed independent review plus the revision-2
editor/citation return in `editor-returns.json`; independent successor acceptance remains pending.
This reconciliation read those records, not runtime/test bodies or original standards anew.

## Unresolved findings, decisions and evidence — exact scope retained

Every entry below is indexed down to original candidate facets, source units and reopening paths in
the companion records. Shared mechanisms receive one exact-facet relationship; different storage,
actor, phase or caller responsibilities retain separate questions.

| Retained question | Exact original scope / reopening condition |
| --- | --- |
| Metadata ownership/decoding/cache | A C003–C006/C016/C017/C021 and Management X002: timeout alias/equality/hash, FIPS tag mapping/width, flagged form factor, wider capability bits, raw representation and evidence expiry. Stronger ownership/stability or decoding claims require their recorded decision/evidence; corrected prose changes none of them. |
| Native/connection/listener lifetimes | B1 C002–C006/C009–C012; B3 C002/C005/C006; B4 C001/C002/C003/C005/C006/C009: early context cleanup, cadence, partial startup, post-open logger cleanup, custom versus successful-deferred Windows disposal, context flow, admission precedence, exact declarations and backend interpretation. Native pending, terminal, drained and release proven stay distinct. |
| Complete workflow/callback ownership | B5 C006 and actual nine-boundary callers: one Core exchange guard supplies no whole public-operation/ceremony lease. Reset/cache, detached callbacks, post-exchange parsing and sequential applet operations retain their actual owners. PIV's callbacks outside its guard differ from OTP's self-wait path. |
| Input and layered sensitive storage | C input/TLV/crypto concerns, B4 C007, B5 C005, B6 C002 and each applet: UTF-16/code-point/UTF-8/profile enforcement, redirected strings, independent copies, exceptional cleanup, report ownership and read-only result clearing need their exact policy/owner. Public metadata/status alone is not secret by direction. |
| Wire/profile/state | B5 raw grammar/control/recovery/version and B6 C001/C003–C012/C015/C016: Le/remaining-command limits, partial failures, counter mutation/phase latch, later INS82, startup cleanup/DEK, parameter clones, SCP11 profile/trust, protected chaining, reselect, KeyReference and ATR value semantics remain separate. Use the corrected selected-level conditions above. |
| Applet reset/auth/version | SD omitted reset options/raw bypass, HSM/OpenPGP retained graph/plain reselect, Management family/reset-success state and OATH's different terminal RESET contract retain distinct policies. Setup flags supply no ongoing channel health, applet PIN/UV/lock authorization or device-phase proof. |
| CTAP/WebAuthn applet requirements | All old CTAP/WA aliases survive. WA-IMP-010 descriptor recovery remains separate from resolved descriptor prose; CTAP-DEC-002 native DTO/platform/browser/RP serializer intent still needs maintainer decision. No field stripping is authorized. PIN peer/profile, ARKG wire/math, response/envelope/blob/parser/range and extension policies remain their actual applet owners. |
| HSM format and external authentication | HSM-IMP-008 / HSM X005 retains historical supplied-cryptogram **56 versus 48 bytes**, unknown raw key/tail regions, firmware/response grammar and result/receipt ownership. Omitted-cryptogram three-key agreement is different from successful HSM/connector enrollment, peer verification, host authentication and protected commands. |
| PIV/OpenPGP confirmed applet/tool scopes | **PIVIMP-005 remains confirmed/unfixed**: actual tool RSA failed original-message verification; Ed25519 verified SHA256(message); direct SDK controls passed. OpenPGP's historical PIN/KDF identity, X25519 framing and ATT read findings remain confirmed for their recorded scopes. Core catalog/owner prose supplies no repair. |
| Test/sample/tooling scope | Actual fixture, assertion-failure drain, cleanup, output/argv, input/certificate/result and semantic-oracle questions retain their original IDs. A compiler result, method name, callback count or disposal invocation supplies no unobserved lifetime/erasure/restoration. Source descriptions can be corrected without treating those runtime questions as fixed or intended policy. |
| Source/native/provider/deployment evidence | Original NIST-PIV PDF, final NIST table/sample archive bytes, missing Rust/generator/comparator captures, final SCP11/vendor/ISO clauses, exact installed NativeShims producer/header/flags, actual providers and historical platform artifacts retain bounded gaps. Published source or local headers identify no loaded producer. |

These are deferred status/evidence entries, not a selected implementation backlog. Questions with no
new implementation defect remain explicit qualifications or referrals, rather than open bugs counted
from every dimension. All earlier proposed experiments remain **unexecuted**; none is implemented,
rescheduled or newly authorized by this handoff.

## Resolutions, retraction and physical limits protected

- All **14 OATH IMP resolutions** retain their precise source scopes, including seed/Base32/input,
  raw VALIDATE/calculation cleanup and terminal RESET. OATH DEC-001's provenance correction is resolved
  while broader failure usability remains open; DEC-005 timestamp policy stays resolved. Other URI,
  raw-key, padding, HOTP and firmware-rationale questions retain their old scope. Lower Core copies,
  workflow or SCP evidence do not reopen the fourteen fixes wholesale.
- **CTAP-XREF-001 / WA-XREF-001** remain documentation-resolved for their User/descriptor prose.
  Recovery and disclosure intent keep their different IDs. All 21 PGP-DEP labels remain documentation
  dependencies, outside new Core bug counts.
- **HSM retry-message mismatch: RETRACTED.** The helper and asymmetric retry test both use
  `Invalid credential password`. Preserve `corrections.md` and the failed checker history. This is no
  open bug or reason to reopen historical passing evidence. X007's actual exception XML and diagnostic/
  test-oracle concerns remain separate.
- PIV's exact older fixes, source-confirmed PIVIMP-009 date issue, PIVIMP-010 object encoding and other
  retained uncertainties stay in `protected-dispositions.json`; historical PIV 86/89 canonical methods
  and supplemental outcomes keep their original rig/profile/restore limitations. OpenPGP's fourteen
  engineering groups, HSM's eight and OTP's twelve retain their definitions and current source scope.
- SCP03 **1.1.2 Public Release** is distinct from code-cited **1.1.2.6 Public Review**. Retained SCP11
  **1.3.0.13 Public Review** supplies draft-specific actor/phase evidence; final 1.4 publication does not
  supply inspected final clauses or a complete YubiKey profile. Independent exact-source acceptance
  remains required at the qualified locators and conditions.
- B4's PCI discrepancy is conditional on the published selected **Linux LP64** producer/header route:
  native two unsigned longs versus managed two four-byte values. Windows uses two 32-bit DWORDs;
  macOS framework selection needs its own producer/header evidence. This supplies no all-OS mismatch
  claim, installed-producer identity or observed transmit failure.
- Serial **9681620** remains the unexplained historical two-key abandoned HID read. Serial **125** had
  two `6A88` results during INITIALIZE UPDATE, **before EXTERNAL AUTHENTICATE and RESET**. Plain or
  synthetic success supplies no missing secure-reset execution.
- The user's Windows CCID/HID ready handoff remains **unready/unreviewed** and requires its separate
  pinned delta/impact review when supplied. It leaves truthful current-baseline documentation available
  for review. PIV physical touch/hotplug and touch-dependent cancellation/recovery remain **deferred**.
  No new device, native, credential, reset or crypto operation was requested or performed.

## Verification and closeout boundary

The records-only join verifies **14,044 disjoint assigned IDs**, all **185 original candidate IDs**,
all **100 inherited rows / 70 groups / 21 labels**, and the earlier-map preservation hashes. Original
bytes for **1,397 pinned paths** and **14,041 original ranges** reconcile through pinned Git objects.
The remaining three ranges are the explicitly post-pin Core campaign handoff metadata; their original
inventory/range identities remain retained, without fictitious source-pin byte proof. The exact
candidate-to-document map covers **859 associated paths** and names current edit owners, returned
decisions and pending cases. No central coverage file was changed.

This worker ran record/schema/hash/Git-object checks only. It edited no product, assertions, API,
central registry/coverage, Git index/ref or prior map; it started no subagent, SDK build/test/formatter,
native/device/crypto run or implementation project. Current raw documentation hashes are recorded
separately from source evidence, with the A/C accepted-transfer comparison made explicitly.

Remaining Pass‑1 gates are exact successor reviews, completed remaining editor/path dispositions,
coordinator integration, source/example/compiler validation at final identities, required sampling,
fresh final evidence acceptance and publication/handoff. This draft claims none of those complete.
After the agreed Core Pass‑1 publication and deferred handoff, **stop**.
